<title>USA: US banks free rsrvs $1.063 bln/day June 18 two wk.</title>
<headline>US banks free rsrvs $1.063 bln/day June 18 two wk.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-06-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>U.S. commercial banks had free reserves of $1.063 billion per day in the two weeks ended June 18, versus revised free reserves of $967 million in the previous two-week period, the Federal Reserve said.</p>
<p>Seasonal borrowings were $205 million versus $210 million a day. Extended credits were nil.</p>
<p>(( -- N.A. Treasury Desk, 212-859-1660 ))</p>
